---
Fix integer overflow in export calculations.

Large export durations or high sample rates can cause integer overflow
in buffer size calculations, leading to undersized allocations and
buffer overflows.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All buffer size calculations use size_t or uint64_t where appropriate
- [ ] Overflow checks before multiplication (num_frames * channels * bytes_per_sample)
- [ ] Export refuses gracefully if calculated size exceeds reasonable limits
- [ ] WAV header size fields handled correctly for large files

## Test Plan
- [ ] Export a long project (e.g. 60 minutes), verify correct file size
- [ ] Export at high sample rate (96kHz), verify no overflow
- [ ] Test with edge case durations that would overflow 32-bit math
